# Pull client logic out of GeneratedScripts

Any analysis or edit that reads or changes `GeneratedScripts.cpp`, `GeneratedScripts.h`, or a caller of those functions includes an extract audit in the same reply.

The audit is the whole feature, not only the function that was asked about. Include the callers, the callees, and the other functions on that screen or flow.

For each chunk, name the functions and one existing destination (`core/gameplay`, `core/network`, `core/ui`, `core/world`). A refactor or a rewrite is fine.

Removing a chunk deletes it from `GeneratedScripts.cpp`. Do not leave a forwarding call there. Define the function in the destination file. A caller that only exists to reach that function moves with it. The audit names any call that remains, and that call is the interpreter dispatching a virtual or a tick. It is not a wrapper.

New behavior is not added to the generated file. The generated file stays the interpreter.
